    "result_text": "The build succeeds and both acceptance tests pass. Here's a summary of what I implemented for the owner soft-delete change.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Domain model** \u2014 `model/Owner.java`\n- Added a nullable `deleted` column (`@Column(name = \"deleted\")`) initialized to `false`, with a `getDeleted()` that normalizes `null` \u2192 `false` (so owners persisted before the column existed, and newly created owners, both read as not-deleted) and a `setDeleted(...)`.\n\n**Database schema** \u2014 `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`\n- Added a `deleted BOOLEAN` column to the `owners` table. The tests run on HSQLDB with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the schema; I updated all four platforms for consistency.\n\n**API contract** \u2014 `resources/openapi.yml`\n- Added a read-only `deleted` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto.getDeleted()`/`setDeleted()`. MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` auto-maps it, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `deleted`.\n\n**Controller** \u2014 `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`\n- `deleteOwner`: instead of removing the row, it now sets `deleted = true` and saves the owner, retaining the record and returning `204 No Content` (2xx).\n- Added an `isNotDeleted(Owner)` helper and applied it to the create endpoint's duplicate/identity checks \u2014 `rejectDuplicateIdentity`, `rejectHouseholdDuplicate`, and `applyPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 so owners flagged deleted no longer block or taint a new owner.\n\n## Verification\n- `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` \u2014 new owner reads `deleted: false`; after DELETE, `GET` still returns the owner with `deleted: true`. \u2705\n- `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` \u2014 re-creating an owner whose only match is soft-deleted succeeds. \u2705\n- `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nOne note: `ClinicService.deleteOwner` (the hard-delete) is now unused by the controller but left in place, as it's part of the service interface and nothing in the spec asked to remove it.",
